      "id": "priority_update_receive_setup",
      "change_ids": [
        "g0020"
      ],
      "kind": "configuration",
      "necessary": true,
      "established": true,
      "requirement": "Enable built-in PRIORITY_UPDATE reception and advertise local SETTINGS_NO_RFC7540_PRIORITIES=1 so the server receiver can process a valid PRIORITY_UPDATE frame.",
      "target_route": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput creates a server, submits SETTINGS, then passes input to nghttp2_session_mem_recv. A valid client preface, initial SETTINGS, and PRIORITY_UPDATE frame should reach session_process_priority_update_frame.",
      "failure_condition": "The null-option session has a zero built-in extension mask. Its sole submitted setting is MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS, which sets pending_no_rfc7540_priorities to 0. The receiver therefore ignores PRIORITY_UPDATE before unpacking, updating a stream, or calling the frame callback.",
      "alternative_paths": "Peer SETTINGS changes remote settings, not the pending local setting. The user-extension route also requires an option and unpack callback absent from the complete harness. Raw input cannot change either setup.",
